{"kind":"assert","text":"Planner decision on d553ff29 (A1c: credential-bearing membership history and archives).\n\n1. New membership cohort, no backward compatibility: invitations carry an invitation public key instead of inviteHash. join and enrol carry a signature by the invitation private key over (scope, invitation id, joining key id), not the secret. No signed entry in the new cohort holds a credential, so archives copy every entry unchanged and native continuity holds. The secret given to the invitee is the invitation private key (or a seed for it); it never enters a signed entry.\n2. Scopes in the current cohort (inline secret in join/enrol) are not archivable. Archive export refuses them whole with a named reason (unsupported-credential-cohort). No skipping, redaction or rewriting of entries. The privacy requirement in 15.3/J2 stays as written.\n3. Initial export policy v1 is an allowlist, refusal by default: the new membership cohort, and generic declarations whose definition digests the checker certifies in the A1 review as carrying no credential or private fields. Custom domains and foreign entry copies are refused whole in v1. Because v1 refuses rather than omits, it needs no omission metadata; omission is a later versioned policy.\n4. Order: the membership cohort change is its own Source request under e871ba09 (I will file it); A1 layout and A0a/A0b proceed in parallel; credential-bearing histories stay disabled until the new cohort lands."}